WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:09.875
Frank and Lisa were enjoying ice-cream cones with their grandpa.

2
00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:14.579
"How's your ice cream, Grandpa?" asked Lisa.

3
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.228
"It's delicious," Grandpa replied.

4
00:00:18.229 --> 00:00:26.573
"As soon as we're finished with our ice cream, why don't we all go to watch the fireflies?"

5
00:00:26.574 --> 00:00:28.386
Frank and Lisa agreed.

6
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:31.474
They all went out to the trees behind the ice-cream shop.

7
00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:35.159
It was dusk, and fireflies were everywhere.

8
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.303
"Look! I caught a firefly!" shouted Frank.

9
00:00:40.304 --> 00:00:44.443
"Why does it glow?" Lisa asked.

10
00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:52.462
"I don't know. Grandpa, what makes a firefly glow?" Frank asked.

11
00:00:52.463 --> 00:00:57.002
"That's a good question, Frank," said Grandpa.

12
00:00:57.003 --> 00:01:04.953
"Fireflies have a chemical in their stomach that glows when it comes in contact with oxygen.

13
00:01:04.954 --> 00:01:11.036
Did you also know that only the male fireflies glow?" Grandpa asked.

14
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:15.264
"No, why is that?" said Frank.

15
00:01:15.265 --> 00:01:21.503
"The male firefly glows to attract the female fireflies.

16
00:01:21.504 --> 00:01:28.971
The faster he flickers, the more likely he will attract a female firefly," Grandpa explained.

17
00:01:28.972 --> 00:01:34.574
"Wow, you know so much about fireflies!" said Lisa.

18
00:01:34.575 --> 00:01:38.519
Lisa and Frank's parents and Grandma joined them.

19
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:44.425
"When I was your age," contintued Grandpa, "we used to light our house with fireflies."

20
00:01:44.426 --> 00:01:48.056
"Really?" shouted Lisa and Frank.

21
00:01:48.057 --> 00:01:54.291
"No," said Mom. "He's telling a tall tale."

22
00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:58.987
"It's getting late," said Grandma. "We should go."

23
00:01:58.988 --> 00:02:01.975
"Okay," Grandpa replied.

24
00:02:01.976 --> 00:02:05.923
"Everybody in the back of the truck, and remember the rules:

25
00:02:05.924 --> 00:02:12.284
No standing up and no sticking your hands outside the truck."

26
00:02:12.285 --> 00:02:15.360
Grandpa drove them safely home.

27
00:02:15.361 --> 00:02:18.773
"We're home," said Grandpa.

28
00:02:18.774 --> 00:02:24.235
"And your grandma and I have a surprise for you kids."

29
00:02:24.236 --> 00:02:27.296
Grandma led them to a bedroom and opened the door.

30
00:02:27.297 --> 00:02:29.464
Inside were bunk beds.

31
00:02:29.465 --> 00:02:34.549
"Your grandpa made these beds for you," said Grandma.

32
00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:40.301
"Cool," said Frank. "I'm sleeping in the top bunk."

33
00:02:40.302 --> 00:02:44.912
"I want to sleep in the top bunk," whined Lisa.

34
00:02:44.913 --> 00:02:50.118
"I'm sorry, Lisa," said Grandpa, "but Frank is older.

35
00:02:50.119 --> 00:02:52.111
He should sleep in the top bunk.

36
00:02:52.112 --> 00:02:55.036
Do you need help climbing up?"

37
00:02:55.037 --> 00:02:59.840
"No, but can you hand Terry to me?" asked Frank.

38
00:02:59.841 --> 00:03:02.585
"Terry?" Grandpa asked.

39
00:03:02.586 --> 00:03:09.007
"Terry is Frank's Tyrannosaurus rex," said Mom with a laugh.

40
00:03:09.008 --> 00:03:15.844
"Yeah, Terry is so ugly that he scares all the monsters away," added Frank.

41
00:03:15.845 --> 00:03:18.816
He had climbed up into bed.

42
00:03:18.817 --> 00:03:23.472
"Oh, I see," replied Grandpa as he handed Terry to Frank.

43
00:03:23.473 --> 00:03:26.160
"But there are no monsters in this house.

44
00:03:26.161 --> 00:03:29.764
I chased them all away when your mom was little."

45
00:03:29.765 --> 00:03:32.898
"It's true," said Mom.

46
00:03:32.899 --> 00:03:37.568
"Your grandpa is very good at scaring away monsters.

47
00:03:37.569 --> 00:03:42.878
Good night. I'll leave the door open and the hall light on."

48
00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:45.512
"Good night, Mom," said Frank.

49
00:03:45.513 --> 00:03:48.520
"Good night," said Lisa.

50
00:03:48.521 --> 00:03:52.032
In the middle of night, Frank dropped his dinosaur.

51
00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:56.777
"Oh, Terry! Are you okay?" he whispered.

52
00:03:56.778 --> 00:03:59.105
"Terry, are you okay?

53
00:03:59.106 --> 00:04:01.870
Are you scared?" said Lisa.

54
00:04:01.871 --> 00:04:04.607
Frank climbed down to get Terry.

55
00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:09.009
"Can Terry and I sleep with you and Dolly?" asked Frank.

56
00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:11.921
"Terry is afraid of the top bunk."

57
00:04:11.922 --> 00:04:18.449
"Okay," said Lisa sleepily. "Make sure Terry doesn't eat Dolly."

58
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.213
"He won't," promised Frank.

59
00:04:21.214 --> 00:04:25.218
In the morning, Grandpa and Mom came to wake them up.

60
00:04:25.219 --> 00:04:28.114
"Frank, Lisa, it's time to get up.

61
00:04:28.115 --> 00:04:31.374
We're going to the lake," said Grandpa.

62
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:36.328
"Okay," said Frank and Lisa.

63
00:04:36.329 --> 00:04:41.305
"Frank, why are you sleeping with Lisa?" asked Mom.

64
00:04:41.306 --> 00:04:44.984
"Terry fell out of the top bunk," said Frank.

65
00:04:44.985 --> 00:04:49.350
"I climbed down to get him, but he was too scared to go back.

66
00:04:49.351 --> 00:04:52.388
So we slept with Lisa."

67
00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:55.010
"It's true," replied Lisa.

68
00:04:55.011 --> 00:04:58.477
"And Terry promised not to eat Dolly."

69
00:04:58.478 --> 00:05:00.533
Everyone smiled.
